@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] comment-only-contract-review
Automated contract reviews submit only `COMMENT` reviews pinned to the inspected PR head; they
never approve a PR or request changes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-notifications
For an edited or removed existing contract, the review MUST cc its owners at that contract unless
the same change was already notified. Edits use both old and new owners; removals use old owners.
New contracts MUST NOT produce owner notifications.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-violation-recipients
Each newly reported violation MUST cc the violated contract's `notify` recipients. Owners MUST NOT
be included unless explicitly listed in `notify`; missing recipients MUST NOT suppress a finding.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-repeat-notifications
Reviews MUST NOT repeat an identical contract-change notification or an unresolved finding unless
the relevant contract or violating behavior has materially changed. Still-valid prior findings
that remain relevant under the skill's verification scope MUST remain in the summary with links
to their existing comments.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-callers
New or changed contracts trigger inspection of callers/references for each affected declaration,
including each inspected caller's applicable contracts; limits materially affecting a finding are
disclosed in that finding's comment.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-summary
Review summaries are `cc: LGTM` when no violations are found, otherwise `cc:` followed by a blank
line and bullets of `**{contract-name}**: {failure_short_description}`, with details in the
associated comments.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-locations
Every review finding identifies the violating source location; locations outside the commentable
PR diff are retained in the review body with source permalinks.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] review-host-services
Review setup MUST NOT change ownership or permissions on host service sockets.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-requests
The review bot requests a contract review when `cc` appears in the leading handle list of an `r?`
line in a new PR description or conversation comment, or an edit introducing that request. Draft
PRs are eligible; pushes and edits retaining an existing request do not request another review.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] contract-review-request-access
Before dispatch or Codex execution, the requester MUST be a human with current repository `write`,
`maintain`, or `admin` permission. The requester is the event sender for direct requests and the
supplied originating run's actor for delegated requests.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] contract-review-pr-eligibility
Request resolution MUST reject a PR that is closed or whose head repository differs from the
caller's repository. Draft status MUST NOT make an otherwise eligible PR ineligible.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] contract-review-dispatch-association
Dispatching automation MUST supply a `request-run-id` belonging to the request for the supplied PR.
This association is a caller precondition; the receiving action does not independently verify it.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-head-workflow
The repository workflow dispatches requested reviews on the PR's head branch, and each dispatched
review inspects the workflow run's commit. Later pushes neither cancel that run nor trigger a new
review; its results remain attached to the inspected commit.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-progress-name
Review commit statuses MUST use names distinct from workflow jobs, including jobs in request-only
runs.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-request-identity
A request with an already-published review for the same request ID and base/head commits MUST be
skipped. A request MUST NOT be skipped solely because another request reviewed the same commits;
delegated retries MUST retain the originating request ID.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-publication
Publication MUST be skipped if the PR has closed. Otherwise, later head or base changes MUST NOT
invalidate a completed review; its context, comment locations, and submitted commit MUST use the
captured comparison.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] contract-review-automation-source
Review handling, prompts, contract tooling, and publication use the selected action revision;
inspected source uses the PR head captured when resolving the request. Local action callers load
the actions from the workflow's revision.
